{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00656",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 2.07,
      "end_seconds": 15.4,
      "duration_seconds": 13.33,
      "text": "Good morning. I'll be as precise as I can, because this is a bit unusual. My cousin died suddenly last month, aged thirty-one, and I'd like to be screened."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.19,
      "end_seconds": 25.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.26,
      "text": "I'm very sorry to hear that. Do you know what the cause was?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.52,
      "end_seconds": 37.8,
      "duration_seconds": 9.28,
      "text": "They say it was his heart, an arrhythmia of some kind. They're still waiting for the full post-mortem results."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.55,
      "end_seconds": 49.27,
      "duration_seconds": 8.72,
      "text": "That must be very hard on the family. And how about you, have you had any symptoms yourself? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.25,
      "end_seconds": 64.05,
      "duration_seconds": 11.8,
      "text": "Possibly. Now and then I get a flutter in my chest, a sort of skipped beat. But I can't say when I first noticed it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.18,
      "end_seconds": 71.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Is it when you're resting, or exercising?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.11,
      "end_seconds": 84.89,
      "duration_seconds": 9.78,
      "text": "Resting, usually. It might have been last year, or the year before, I honestly couldn't tell you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.07,
      "end_seconds": 93.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Do you ever faint, or nearly faint, with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.3,
      "end_seconds": 101.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "No, never. I've never fainted in my life."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.39,
      "end_seconds": 106.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Good. Do you exercise much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.32,
      "end_seconds": 117.96,
      "duration_seconds": 8.64,
      "text": "I run three times a week, five kilometres, and I've never had trouble with it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.0,
      "end_seconds": 128.77,
      "duration_seconds": 7.77,
      "text": "That's reassuring. Any allergies I need to know about before I examine you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.37,
      "end_seconds": 135.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "None at all. No allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.06,
      "end_seconds": 142.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Let me take your pulse and blood pressure. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.63,
      "end_seconds": 146.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Of course. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.88,
      "end_seconds": 165.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "Pulse 62, regular, and blood pressure 118 over 74."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.51,
      "end_seconds": 170.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Is that normal? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.46,
      "end_seconds": 176.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Excellent for a runner. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.95,
      "end_seconds": 184.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "So what do you think the flutter is? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.29,
      "end_seconds": 199.44,
      "duration_seconds": 12.15,
      "text": "A skipped beat at rest, in someone who runs and has a normal pulse, is most likely ectopic beats, which are extra beats and very common."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.33,
      "end_seconds": 206.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Common? So not necessarily a problem? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.13,
      "end_seconds": 218.24,
      "duration_seconds": 9.11,
      "text": "Usually harmless. But with your cousin's history, I don't want to rely on that. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.77,
      "end_seconds": 224.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Quite. That's why I came. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.57,
      "end_seconds": 240.75,
      "duration_seconds": 13.18,
      "text": "I'm going to refer you to the inherited cardiac conditions clinic, and they'll do the right tests, probably an ECG, an echocardiogram, and maybe a heart rhythm monitor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.79,
      "end_seconds": 247.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "And the cousin's results will matter? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.73,
      "end_seconds": 260.43,
      "duration_seconds": 9.7,
      "text": "Very much. Ask the family to share the post-mortem findings with the clinic, they'll want to see them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.54,
      "end_seconds": 271.77,
      "duration_seconds": 8.23,
      "text": "I'll do that. Is there anything I should avoid in the meantime? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.95,
      "end_seconds": 289.66,
      "duration_seconds": 14.71,
      "text": "Carry on as normal, and if you ever faint, or get chest pain with exercise, or a racing heart that won't settle, go to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.85,
      "end_seconds": 296.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "Understood. Thank you for being so thorough. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.3,
      "end_seconds": 306.01,
      "duration_seconds": 6.71,
      "text": "You did the right thing. The clinic will write to you. ~"
    }
  ]
}
